204	/**
205	 * The claims on a sheet: added to a person and edited (amount, date, note). A claim given no date
206	 * takes the sheet's today. A claim starts as DRAFT and moves through its statuses (see
207	 * {@link ClaimStatus}); a change its status does not allow is refused. Only a DRAFT can be edited:
208	 * to change an open claim, void it and add a new one. Settling a claim fixes its
209	 * due at the rate its person's grade has then for the claim's date; an open claim's due stays live.
210	 * A claim records who opened it, and that user cannot settle it (four eyes). A claim bound by its
211	 * person's last statement keeps the figure it had then, and settling it fixes that figure. No claim
212	 * dated inside a closed period can be added, edited (to or from such a date) or change status. No
213	 * claim can be added or edited to a date after its person's retirement date. A clerk settles a claim
214	 * only when its figure is at or below the sheet's clerk limit (a claim with no figure is within any
215	 * limit); a clerk settling one above it makes it PENDING instead. A steward settles any claim, and
216	 * approves a PENDING claim (SETTLED, its due fixed then) or rejects it with a reason (back to OPEN);
217	 * the user who opened a claim cannot approve it. A PENDING claim is not bound by a statement: it
218	 * shows its live figure, and is bound again by the last statement once rejected. A claim's live due is never below the sheet's floor. An
219	 * overdue claim's due gains a late charge on top of its figure (see {@link LateCharge}); a statement
220	 * binds only the figure under it, and settling fixes the charge into the settled due. A claim with
221	 * a negative amount is a correction: it is allowed only when it names, by number, a SETTLED claim
222	 * of the same person that it corrects. Its due has no floor and no late charge. A steward can move
223	 * a DRAFT, OPEN or PENDING claim to another person: it keeps its number and date, loses any figure
224	 * a statement bound it to, and is listed as its new person's newest claim. A steward can re-settle
225	 * a SETTLED claim: its due is fixed again at the figure it would have today as an open claim bound
226	 * by no statement (today's rates, grades, floor and late charge).
227	 */
